  "goal": "Turn RC3 signed local publication into hosted release transport, fleet-ring rollout, remote registry mirroring, and GA-hardening evidence without claiming GA production readiness.",
  "core_thesis": "RC4 proves that signed RC3 release metadata can move through hosted transport and staged fleet operations while all mutation authority remains in AgentCore and SecurityExecutionEngine.",
  "non_goals": [
    "Do not claim GA production readiness.",
    "Do not package or read local private production signing material.",
    "Do not let hosted transport, TUI, model replay, normal shell, or remote control plane mutate active artifacts directly.",
    "Do not treat network reachability as sufficient release proof.",
    "Do not skip rollback, revocation, support redaction, or provenance binding."
  ],
  "primary_acceptance": [
    "Hosted release transport metadata is hash-bound to the RC3 publication manifest, channel index, production verification, and signing/publication gate.",
    "Remote registry mirror replay can prove mirror freshness, trust, rollback baseline, and fail-closed handling for tamper, stale, missing, or untrusted mirror data.",
    "Fleet-ring rollout plans are staged, bounded by exact operator approval, and route every side effect through AgentCore PlanSpec and SecurityExecutionEngine.",
    "Signed hosted-channel consumers can verify published release metadata without mutating activation state.",
    "Promotion gates fail closed when hosted transport, mirror, fleet ring, rollback, revocation, or support evidence is missing, stale, or mismatched."
  ],
